1
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,359
And the door hinge...

2
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,699
swung open on its own.

3
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,359
Outside...

4
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,559
pitch-black.

5
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:35,740
Just bloody footprints by the doorway,

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,119
drip, drip...

7
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:40,939
leading straight from the door to the bed.

8
00:00:42,159 --> 00:00:43,079
Looking closer,

9
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,759
the quilt was clearly squirming!

10
00:00:46,899 --> 00:00:48,000
Bulging up,

11
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,500
twitching and shaking.

12
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:50,899
Turns out...

13
00:00:53,439 --> 00:00:55,240
it was the neighbor's calico cat!

14
00:00:55,539 --> 00:00:56,659
It fell into a mud ditch,

15
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:57,780
climbed back out,

16
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,119
and slipped under the quilt, rubbing itself dry!

17
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:01,759
Chen Daguang...

18
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,219
You're cracking me up!

19
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:05,700
Power's back!

20
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:07,719
Man...

21
00:01:07,799 --> 00:01:08,540
what kind of crap was that?

22
00:01:08,659 --> 00:01:09,599
The light flicking on was scarier than you.

23
00:01:11,819 --> 00:01:12,459
Ain't that the truth.

24
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:14,180
What a garbage story, seriously.

25
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:15,519
Lame as hell.

26
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,280
For real.

27
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:18,780
I thought some female ghost...

28
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:21,879
possessed a corpse and floated out of the water.

29
00:01:24,159 --> 00:01:24,840
Right?

30
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,879
Maybe it wasn't a cat at all.

31
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,000
She was a drowned ghost from the riverbank!

32
00:01:30,659 --> 00:01:31,540
And then?

33
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,439
She crawled out from underwater,

34
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,579
pried open your door...

35
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,280
And while you were asleep at night,

36
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:39,420
she suddenly slipped into your bed,

37
00:01:39,719 --> 00:01:41,819
swapping your heart, liver, and lungs...

38
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:44,079
all for rotten mud and weeds!

39
00:01:44,219 --> 00:01:45,760
Then your guts and intestines,

40
00:01:45,859 --> 00:01:46,780
she clawed them all out!

41
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:49,799
Cut it out! Don't do that to me!

42
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,959
You're actually creeping me out!

43
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,480
Bro...

44
00:01:51,939 --> 00:01:52,799
Did you hear that?

45
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,519
A cat meowed.

46
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,079
Wait, there actually is one.

47
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,099
Quit messing around! I'm right here!

48
00:01:57,099 --> 00:01:57,599
No, I'm serious!

49
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:58,560
Listen, hear that?

50
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:00,500
Meow.

51
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:01,900
I'm not listening, not listening!

52
00:02:02,019 --> 00:02:02,540
Blah, blah, blah!

53
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:04,719
You're the damn turtle!

54
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:07,719
Come on.

55
00:02:07,859 --> 00:02:08,280
Here.

56
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,419
It's getting late, isn't it?

57
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:16,560
What's the rush?

58
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:17,780
Leaving already?

59
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,780
Don't rush off!

60
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,500
Seriously, let me tell you another good one.

61
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,319
Daguang.

62
00:02:21,639 --> 00:02:22,699
The booze is gone anyway.

63
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,199
Why don't you head upstairs and grab two more?

64
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:24,800
Right!

65
00:02:25,199 --> 00:02:26,099
I'll go get us more booze.

66
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,900
Why don't we go somewhere else to drink?

67
00:02:37,539 --> 00:02:37,960
Get some fresh air.

68
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:42,819
What about my bro?

69
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:49,539
Come on.

70
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,219
Careful, slow down.

71
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:51,819
Where did they go?

72
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:52,740
Run!

73
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:53,819
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

74
00:02:53,979 --> 00:02:54,319
Move it!

75
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:55,199
Get on, get on, hop on!

76
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:57,000
Hop on, hop on!

77
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:57,560
Where are you gonna sit?

78
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,319
Quick, I'll squeeze next to you.

79
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:00,860
Bro, my bad, take me with you!

80
00:03:00,979 --> 00:03:02,240
There's really no room left!

81
00:03:02,379 --> 00:03:02,960
Hold on tight!

82
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,120
Hold on tight!

83
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,560
That's dirty, you bastards!

84
00:03:11,979 --> 00:03:12,740
Come back!

85
00:03:17,419 --> 00:03:18,280
Punks.

86
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,000
Thought you could screw with me?

87
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:21,599
Go on and have your fun!

88
00:03:21,979 --> 00:03:22,840
Look at them, laughing their heads off.

89
00:03:24,939 --> 00:03:26,460
This whole crew would fall apart without me.

90
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,060
Thinking I was scared of ghosts.

91
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:49,379
Come on.

92
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:50,120
Watch your step.

93
00:03:50,139 --> 00:03:50,719
Master San.

94
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:52,599
Master San.

95
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,479
Sorry to disturb your peace this late.

96
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,800
Ziwen's here.

97
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,020
Is...

98
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:00,699
isn't this...

99
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:02,539
I recognize you!

100
00:04:02,819 --> 00:04:04,020
I saw you in the papers!

101
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,840
You... you fought the Japanese devils!

102
00:04:05,939 --> 00:04:07,780
Beat those devils till they wailed!

103
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,120
Me?

104
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,919
I'm just an old guy watching the bathhouse.

105
00:04:11,099 --> 00:04:12,740
No, no, you're an anti-Japanese war hero!

106
00:04:13,159 --> 00:04:13,780
Really!

107
00:04:14,539 --> 00:04:14,960
Master San,

108
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:18,000
could you bend the rules a bit?

109
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:21,879
Since Ziwen asked,

110
00:04:22,199 --> 00:04:23,560
clear the place out and run the water.

111
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:24,740
Scrub the baths!

112
00:04:25,279 --> 00:04:25,660
Come on.

113
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,660
I'll take you to soak in the big baths!

114
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:27,480
Let's go.

115
00:04:27,519 --> 00:04:28,779
Girls get to soak in the big bath too?

116
00:04:29,199 --> 00:04:30,180
It feels amazing!

117
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,620
With them?

118
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,019
You'll see in a minute.

119
00:04:33,759 --> 00:04:34,959
Back then in Songliao,

120
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:36,220
or even across the entire Northeast,

121
00:04:36,579 --> 00:04:37,899
girls only had showers.

122
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:38,980
No soaking baths.

123
00:04:39,519 --> 00:04:40,560
Girls soaking in a big bath?

124
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,040
Nobody had ever heard of such a thing.

125
00:04:42,639 --> 00:04:43,800
Where are they soaking?

126
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:45,620
Next door.

127
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,180
How do you like it?

128
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:56,839
Worker Comrade Liu Haizhu,

129
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:59,180
can you handle these sugar-coated bullets?

130
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:00,860
Decadent.

131
00:05:01,459 --> 00:05:01,959
Degenerate.

132
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,439
Don't be scared.

133
00:05:34,319 --> 00:05:35,079
Keeping busy, Zhao?

134
00:05:35,939 --> 00:05:36,759
Who do you think you're talking to?

135
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,120
If there's anything you want to eat or drink,

136
00:05:39,279 --> 00:05:39,779
or wear or put on,

137
00:05:39,879 --> 00:05:40,660
just tell Brother Ran.

138
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:41,680
Brother Ran will buy it for you.

139
00:05:42,399 --> 00:05:43,779
If you step out of line once you're out...

140
00:05:43,879 --> 00:05:45,540
Even if I do, I'll let you catch me again.

141
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,259
Scumbag.

142
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,240
Nobody came to pick me up?

143
00:05:59,139 --> 00:06:00,180
They're asking for a beating.

144
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:02,660
Didn't you ask me...

145
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:05,180
...where I went after that incident?

146
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,579
I was locked up.

147
00:06:08,379 --> 00:06:08,839
Prison.

148
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,279
Prison?

149
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,160
How is that possible?

150
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:15,540
Weren't you saving someone?

151
00:06:16,839 --> 00:06:18,579
The kid I shot almost didn't make it.

152
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,699
Excessive force resulting in severe injury.

153
00:06:20,899 --> 00:06:21,540
Got three years.

154
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,120
How did you get mixed up in something like this?

155
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:35,860
Life in prison must've been rough, right?

156
00:06:37,339 --> 00:06:38,300
Back then,

157
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,699
I was just a nobody, a poor student.

158
00:06:41,639 --> 00:06:42,420
Old He...

159
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,360
he was a real seasoned hoodlum.

160
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,500
The second I went in, he gave me "special care."

161
00:06:47,639 --> 00:06:48,759
Even after I was transferred to another cell,

162
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,420
he always found ways to reach me.

163
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:51,860
Out in the open, behind my back,

164
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,560
he never gave me a single day of peace.

165
00:06:54,079 --> 00:06:55,439
Then... you just endured it?

166
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:56,600
Endure it?

167
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:57,740
Endure it, and you're dead.

168
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,220
When you can't take it,

169
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,480
all you can do is fight.

170
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:02,220
Each fight added more time to my sentence.

171
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:03,259
Four years in total.

172
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,399
After Brother Ziwen was locked up,

173
00:07:07,779 --> 00:07:08,779
my brother and I

174
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,980
were targeted by the thugs

175
00:07:11,079 --> 00:07:11,680
Old He left behind.

176
00:07:12,439 --> 00:07:14,060
We never had a peaceful day again.

177
00:07:14,839 --> 00:07:16,300
They still gave you trouble?

178
00:07:17,879 --> 00:07:19,420
I had gotten into nursing school back then.

179
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,399
I wanted to be a nurse,

180
00:07:21,519 --> 00:07:22,699
to heal the wounded and save lives.

181
00:07:23,339 --> 00:07:25,600
But rumors spread all over school.

182
00:07:26,319 --> 00:07:27,439
They made it sound like

183
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:30,040
I didn't even deserve to be human.

184
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,500
Then a bunch of

185
00:07:32,579 --> 00:07:33,540
shady thugs

186
00:07:33,959 --> 00:07:35,139
camped outside the school gates,

187
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:36,779
blocking your way home.

188
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,540
Just so you'd see them,

189
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:39,860
just to terrify you.

190
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,339
Gradually,

191
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,980
classmates avoided you,

192
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,939
teachers looked down on you,

193
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,899
and the whole world treated you like a plague.

194
00:07:50,019 --> 00:07:51,139
An invisible dagger like that

195
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:52,759
hurts the most.

196
00:07:53,399 --> 00:07:54,240
Later, on the inside,

197
00:07:54,279 --> 00:07:55,399
I realized one truth.

198
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,100
Only one thing is real:

199
00:07:57,819 --> 00:07:59,839
Whoever has the harder fist calls the shots.

200
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,360
Whoever is ruthless enough

201
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:02,920
gets to survive.

202
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,579
Zhuzi,

203
00:08:10,759 --> 00:08:12,300
you're strong and tough as nails.

204
00:08:13,259 --> 00:08:14,500
You're rare, good material.

205
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,100
But you still don't know how to use it.

206
00:08:16,819 --> 00:08:18,120
Beating up a couple of street thugs

207
00:08:18,279 --> 00:08:19,100
might feel satisfying,

208
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,279
but it doesn't do jack shit.

209
00:08:26,759 --> 00:08:27,399
Me?

210
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,300
I haven't been through what you have,

211
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:33,120
so I don't overthink things like you do.

212
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:34,659
Still,

213
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,000
I just feel...

214
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:41,200
I can't stand seeing folks get pushed around.

215
00:08:41,759 --> 00:08:43,059
I hate seeing honest people get cheated.

216
00:08:43,879 --> 00:08:45,679
I just despise people who bully others.

217
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:49,399
People...

218
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,019
sometimes they're scarier than ghosts.

219
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:56,980
My parents and Brother Ziwen's parents

220
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,000
used to be professors at university.

221
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,480
Back then, they were respected,

222
00:09:01,659 --> 00:09:02,700
prominent figures.

223
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:04,399
But once the storm hit,

224
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,759
the first ones to pounce and tear into you

225
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,840
were always

226
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,779
those who stayed closest to you,

227
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,519
smiling the sweetest.

228
00:09:13,539 --> 00:09:14,019
Zhuzi,

229
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:15,440
remember this:

230
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,580
in this world, if you want to protect anything,

231
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:21,240
a kind heart doesn't do jack shit on its own.

232
00:09:22,059 --> 00:09:23,580
You need ruthless force to back it up.

233
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:25,080
Otherwise, it's completely worthless.

234
00:09:42,639 --> 00:09:43,980
At first, were you

235
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,720
really scared of Brother Ziwen?

236
00:09:46,279 --> 00:09:48,039
Did you think we were totally unreliable,

237
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,259
and couldn't stand the sight of us?

238
00:09:52,879 --> 00:09:53,620
Come on, tell me.

239
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:56,799
A little.

240
00:09:57,779 --> 00:10:00,139
Mainly because of his moniker—

241
00:10:00,519 --> 00:10:01,500
Tyrant of the East.

242
00:10:01,919 --> 00:10:03,080
It made him sound like

243
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,679
some thug who runs rackets

244
00:10:05,759 --> 00:10:07,100
and bullies people all day.

245
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:09,820
But

246
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,700
once I actually got to know you guys,

247
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,460
you were completely different.

248
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:19,539
Zhuzi was right.

249
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,399
You can't judge people by appearances.

250
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:28,600
The ruthlessness is only for outsiders.

251
00:10:30,279 --> 00:10:31,620
Brother Ziwen always says

252
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:34,279
he wants to give us a real home.

253
00:10:35,279 --> 00:10:36,419
To him, though, home

254
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,200
is a fortified fortress

255
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,100
that he has to fight for

256
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,039
and hold up with his fists.

257
00:10:42,919 --> 00:10:44,840
All I want is for everyone to be safe.

258
00:10:45,139 --> 00:10:47,759
As long as we're alive and well,

259
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,279
and stay together,

260
00:10:50,279 --> 00:10:51,740
that's what home means to me.

261
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,419
Zhuzi,

262
00:10:54,259 --> 00:10:55,519
I know you've got fire in you.

263
00:10:56,559 --> 00:10:58,159
You'll risk your life and refuse to yield to fate.

264
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,720
If you don't do something big with me

265
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,100
and carve out an empire,

266
00:11:03,059 --> 00:11:03,740
it'd be a damn waste.

267
00:11:07,919 --> 00:11:10,259
Do big things...

268
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,139
Carve out an empire...

269
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:22,620
Never crossed my mind.

270
00:11:22,659 --> 00:11:24,080
Then start thinking about it now.

271
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,139
Stick with me,

272
00:11:26,139 --> 00:11:27,840
and Songliao will soon be a different place.

273
00:11:28,559 --> 00:11:29,820
You gotta be there to see it.

274
00:11:29,919 --> 00:11:30,879
Together,

275
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,519
we'll turn Songliao

276
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,899
into whatever we want it to be.

277
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,399
You have a home now.

278
00:11:42,779 --> 00:11:44,480
Must be nice. I really envy you.

279
00:11:47,639 --> 00:11:49,519
I've been all by myself here all these years,

280
00:11:49,779 --> 00:11:51,639
never really feeling like I belonged.

281
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,120
I want a home, too.

282
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,000
You will have one.

283
00:12:05,379 --> 00:12:05,940
Still,

284
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:08,779
in the days ahead,

285
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:10,919
how are we supposed to live?

286
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:13,500
I don't know either.

287
00:12:16,399 --> 00:12:17,179
Then again...

288
00:12:18,159 --> 00:12:19,779
you have someone you want to spend them with,

289
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,620
don't you?

290
00:12:41,039 --> 00:12:42,340
You sure you two don't need a ride back?

291
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,639
We're good. You guys head back.

292
00:12:50,679 --> 00:12:51,220
Alright.

293
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,220
They haven't had it easy.

294
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:04,500
It's really nice.

295
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,399
We've got it pretty good too.

296
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:39,059
You're stepping on me.

297
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,740
You're stepping on my shadow.

298
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,519
Wait, come on...

299
00:13:47,379 --> 00:13:48,820
Look, comrade,

300
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:51,440
aren't you picking on me a bit too much?

301
00:13:52,419 --> 00:13:53,240
So what if I pick on you?

302
00:13:53,659 --> 00:13:54,379
You can't.

303
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,120
Th-Then I'll pick on you too.
